── Mulder, by way of MaRa (Apache License 2.0) ────────────────────────────

Atlas inherits work from Mulder (https://github.com/calebevans/mulder,
commit 1246de42), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, by way of
MaRa. What remains in each file below is described as precisely as we can
state it; several of the originally ported parts have since been replaced and
are named as such.

- core/evidence_index.py: the ingestion shape — chunking a tool's full output
  into windows and inserting them in batches (server/extract_helpers.py) —
  and the decision to serialise every write to the per-case database rather
  than let callers contend (db.py `_WriteQueue`; here a module lock, the same
  guarantee without a thread). The FTS5 query sanitiser and the timestamp
  reader that were ported from those files have been replaced: the sanitiser
  now scans the query into typed pieces and handles unterminated quotes and
  dangling operators, and the timestamp reader is a table of the three forms
  the index reads, read by one loop.
- tools/coverage_audit.py: the idea of auditing coverage before the report is
  written, and the names of the two audits (server/tools/review.py:
  audit_tool_coverage, audit_evidence_coverage). The computation behind both
  has been replaced. Breadth is now measured against Atlas's versioned tool
  capability manifest, selected by the evidence classes the case itself
  declares, rather than by diffing an evidence-type-to-tool table; and the
  second audit reports calls no finding was built from, using Atlas's exact
  finding lineage rather than matching source names.
- tools/export_tools.py: emitting an ATT&CK Navigator layer
  (report/navigator.py) and a STIX 2.1 bundle with a flat IOC CSV
  (report/ioc_export.py). Both output shapes are external specifications, so
  the resemblance is largely the specifications'. What fills them is Atlas's:
  gate-validated techniques, confidence-tier eligibility, its own indicator
  extraction, and the STIX relationship direction corrected to
  indicator --indicates--> attack-pattern.

